## Core Requirements
- All rules must include complete metadata
- All rules must follow the established template
- All rules must include clear examples
- All rules must specify related rules and inheritance
- All rules must include maintenance procedures
- All rules must use consistent formatting
- All rules must specify versioning
- All rules must use proper frontmatter
- All rules must indicate their scope (globs)
- All rules must specify if they should always apply

## File Structure Requirements
- All rule files must use the `.mdc` extension
- All rule files must be organized in the appropriate directories
- All rule files must be named according to convention (kebab-case)
- All top-level categories must have their own directory
- Related rules should be grouped in subdirectories
- Meta rules must be in the `_meta` directory
- Index files must be named `index.mdc`
- Configuration files must be named with their purpose

## Metadata Requirements
- All rules must include a description
- All rules must include a version
- All rules must include applicable globs
- All rules must specify if they should always apply
- All rules must list related rules
- All rules must include tags for searchability
- All rules should specify what they extend, if applicable

## Maintenance Procedures
- All rules must be reviewed monthly
- All rules must be updated when dependencies change
- All rules must include migration guides for breaking changes
- All rules must maintain backward compatibility when possible
- All rules must be versioned according to semver
- All rule updates must be documented in version history
- All rules must have a clear deprecation policy

## Validation Requirements
- All rules must be validated for metadata completeness
- All rules must be validated for proper inheritance
- All examples must be validated for accuracy
- All links must be verified
- All structure must be validated against templates
- All rules must be validated for security considerations

